---
import SectionHeading from "../components/SectionHeading.astro"
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"

const baseUrl = "https://data.filecoindataportal.xyz"
---

<Layout
    title="Documentation | Filecoin Data Portal"
    description="Data sources and usage patterns for Filecoin Data Portal datasets."
>
    <section class="page-header" aria-labelledby="docs-title">
        <h1 id="docs-title">Documentation</h1>
        <p>Where the data comes from and how to use it.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="docs">
        <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Documentation sections">
            <a href="#sources-title">Data Sources</a>
            <a href="#using-datasets">Using Datasets</a>
            <a href="#related-tools">Related Tools</a>
        </nav>

        <section id="sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
            <SectionHeading id="sources-title" label="Data Sources" />

            <p>
                Datasets are rebuilt daily from these sources. Each asset declares
                its source in the <a
                    href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal/tree/main/assets"
                    >asset code</a
                >.
            </p>

            <dl class="docs-list">
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://github.com/filecoin-project/lily">Lily</a>
                    </dt>
                    <dd>
                        Chain data on BigQuery: power, sectors, rewards, fees, and
                        messages.
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://docs.filecoin.io/reference/json-rpc"
                            >Filecoin JSON-RPC</a
                        >
                    </dt>
                    <dd>
                        Current storage provider state and PDP registry reads, from
                        Glif, Chain.love, and ChainUp nodes.
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>RIBA chain archive</dt>
                    <dd>
                        Daily <code>eth_getBlockReceipts</code> dumps from
                        <code>chain.data.riba.plus</code>, the source of all FEVM
                        event logs.
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://github.com/FilOzone/filecoin-services"
                            >Filecoin Services</a
                        >
                    </dt>
                    <dd>
                        Contract deployments, plus <a
                            href="https://filecoin.blockscout.com/">Blockscout</a
                        > ABIs, to decode Filecoin Pay, Warm Storage, and PDP events.
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>PDP provider registry</dt>
                    <dd>Provider names, status, and endorsements.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://coincodex.com/crypto/filecoin/">CoinCodex</a>
                    </dt>
                    <dd>Daily FIL price, volume, and market cap.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://www.opensource.observer/"
                            >Open Source Observer</a
                        >
                    </dt>
                    <dd>Public goods funding deployments.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><a href="https://api.filecoin.io/docs">Filecoin API</a></dt>
                    <dd>Current Warm Storage data sets and Filecoin Pay rails.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><a href="https://probelab.io/filecoin/foc/">ProbeLab / Dealbot</a></dt>
                    <dd>Storage, retrieval, and pull checks. These are probe observations, not all client traffic.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><a href="https://defillama.com/chain/filecoin">DefiLlama</a></dt>
                    <dd>DeFi TVL, USDFC supply, and GLIF iFIL yield, dated by snapshot time.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><a href="https://filecoin.blockscout.com/">Blockscout traces</a></dt>
                    <dd>Fee-auction calls used to value FIL in quarterly Filecoin Pay Volume.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
            <p>
                The <a href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal/blob/main/docs/data-sources.md">Filecoin data sources guide</a>
                compares additional APIs, indexers, and RPC endpoints, including access details and limits.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section id="usage" aria-labelledby="using-datasets">
            <SectionHeading id="using-datasets" label="Using Datasets" />

            <p>
                Every dataset in the <a href="/datasets">catalog</a> is published
                daily as a Parquet file. Any Parquet-capable tool can read it
                directly from:
            </p>
            <pre><code>{`${baseUrl}/<dataset>.parquet`}</code></pre>
            <p>
                Dates are UTC. Units and definitions are documented for each column.
                Null values mean unavailable or undefined, not zero; gaps in the
                source archive leave dependent metrics unavailable.
            </p>

            <h3>DuckDB</h3>
            <p>
                Run it in the DuckDB CLI or in the browser with <a
                    href="https://sql-workbench.com/">SQL Workbench</a
                >.
            </p>
            <pre><code>{`select date, onboarded_pibs, raw_power_pibs
from '${baseUrl}/daily_network_metrics.parquet'
order by date desc
limit 7;`}</code></pre>

            <h3>Python</h3>
            <pre><code>{`import polars as pl

df = pl.read_parquet(
    "${baseUrl}/miners.parquet"
)`}</code></pre>

            <h3>JavaScript</h3>
            <p>
                <code>daily_network_metrics</code> is also published as JSON for
                dashboards.
            </p>
            <pre><code>{`const url = "${baseUrl}/daily_network_metrics.json"
const rows = await (await fetch(url)).json()`}</code></pre>

            <h3>Whole database</h3>
            <p>All public tables are available in one DuckDB file, for DuckDB 2.0 or newer:</p>
            <pre><code>{`attach '${baseUrl}/fdp.duckdb' as fdp (read_only);
use fdp;
show tables;`}</code></pre>

            <h3 id="agents">AI agents</h3>
            <p>
                Point your agent to <a href="/SKILL.md">SKILL.md</a> or <a
                    href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a
                > to find, query, and chart the datasets.
            </p>

            <h3>Dashboards</h3>
            <p>
                <a href="/numbers">Filecoin In Numbers</a> is built on the same datasets. See the <a
                    href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal"
                    >source code</a
                >.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section aria-labelledby="related-tools">
            <SectionHeading id="related-tools" label="Related Tools" />

            <dl class="docs-list">
                <div>
                    <dt><a href="https://filfox.info">Filfox</a></dt>
                    <dd>Chain explorer.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://filecoin.blockscout.com/">Blockscout</a>
                    </dt>
                    <dd>FEVM explorer.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://dashboard.starboard.ventures/dashboard"
                            >Starboard</a
                        >
                    </dt>
                    <dd>Network dashboards.</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt>
                        <a href="https://docs.filecoin.io/networks/mainnet/rpcs"
                            >Public RPCs</a
                        >
                    </dt>
                    <dd>Mainnet JSON-RPC endpoints.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>

            <p>
                Missing a source or tool? <a
                    href="https://github.com/davidgasquez/filecoin-data-portal/issues/new"
                    >Open an issue</a
                >.
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>

<style>
    .docs {
        max-inline-size: 72ch;
        margin-inline: auto;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .docs section + section {
        margin-block-start: var(--space-7);
    }

    .docs :global(.section-title) {
        margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
    }

    .docs h3 {
        margin-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-2);
        font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .docs p {
        margin-block: 0 var(--space-3);
        text-wrap: pretty;
    }

    .docs p code,
    .docs dd code {
        padding: 0.05em 0.3em;
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        background: var(--color-surface);
        font-size: 0.9em;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .docs pre {
        margin-block: 0 var(--space-4);
        padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
        overflow-x: auto;
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        background: var(--color-surface);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
        line-height: 1.55;
    }

    .docs pre code {
        background: none;
        padding: 0;
    }

    .docs-list {
        margin-block: var(--space-4) var(--space-4);
        border-block-start: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .docs :global(.section-title) + .docs-list {
        margin-block-start: 0;
        border-block-start: 0;
    }

    .docs-list > div {
        display: grid;
        gap: var(--space-1) var(--space-4);
        padding-block: var(--space-3);
        border-block-end: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }

    .docs-list dt {
        font-weight: 700;
    }

    .docs-list dd {
        margin: 0;
    }

    @media (min-width: 40rem) {
        .docs-list > div {
            grid-template-columns: 22ch 1fr;
        }
    }
</style>
